---
title: Settings
description: Choose how Convrtr looks and works for you. Changes save straight away, in this browser only.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
sidebarPanel: settings
settingsGroups:
  - { id: appearance, title: Appearance }
  - { id: tools, title: Tools }
  - { id: categories, title: Category pages }
  - { id: data, title: Your data }
---
{#-
    Settings, in groups listed in the sidebar panel (partials/panels/settings.njk), and as chips above the groups when
    the panel isn't showing. Each setting saves as soon as it changes, with the same keys and values as the control
    elsewhere that sets it (the navbar's theme menu, the sidebar toggle, each tool's Live typing switch and each
    section's collapse button), so the two always agree. assets/js/site/settings.js wires it up.
#}
{%- from "macros/delimiter.njk" import delimiter %}
{%- macro savedNote(id) %}<span class="setting__saved" data-saved="{{ id }}" aria-hidden="true">Saved</span>{% endmacro %}
{%- macro switchSetting(id, name, hint) %}
<div class="setting">
    <div class="setting__text">
        <label class="setting__name" for="{{ id }}">{{ name }}</label>
        <small class="setting__hint" id="{{ id }}-hint">{{ hint }}</small>
    </div>
    <div class="setting__end">
        {{ savedNote(id) }}
        <div class="form-check form-switch setting__control">
            <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="{{ id }}" aria-describedby="{{ id }}-hint">
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}
<section id="settings" class="section">
    <div class="settings py-4 px-3 px-sm-4" data-settings>
        <nav class="settings-nav" aria-label="Settings groups">
            {%- for group in settingsGroups %}
            <a class="filter-chip" href="#{{ group.id }}" data-settings-link="{{ group.id }}">{{ group.title }}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
        </nav>

        <section class="settings-group" id="appearance" aria-labelledby="appearance-title">
            <h2 class="settings-group__title" id="appearance-title"><i class="bi bi-palette" aria-hidden="true"></i>Appearance</h2>
            <p class="settings-group__intro">How the site looks.</p>
            <div class="setting">
                <div class="setting__text">
                    <span class="setting__name" id="settingTheme-label">Theme</span>
                    <small class="setting__hint" id="settingTheme-hint">Auto follows your device. The theme menu in the navbar sets the same thing.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="setting__end">
                {{ savedNote("settingTheme") }}
                <div class="setting-segments setting__control" role="group" aria-labelledby="settingTheme-label" aria-describedby="settingTheme-hint" id="settingTheme">
                    <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-value="auto"><i class="bi bi-circle-half" aria-hidden="true"></i>Auto</button>
                    <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-value="light"><i class="bi bi-sun-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i>Light</button>
                    <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-value="dark"><i class="bi bi-moon-stars-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i>Dark</button>
                </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            {{ switchSetting("settingPanel", "Show the tool list beside the sidebar", "The list of a category's tools, next to the icons on the left, on wider screens. The button at the top left does the same.") }}
            {{ switchSetting("settingReduceMotion", "Reduce motion", "Turns off the site's animations, such as folds opening and the sidebar sliding, even if your device doesn't ask for less motion.") }}
            {{ switchSetting("settingCompact", "Compact layout", "Tighter spacing around page headings, tools and their boxes, so more of a tool fits on screen. Buttons stay 44px tall for touch.") }}
        </section>

        <section class="settings-group" id="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
            <h2 class="settings-group__title" id="tools-title"><i class="bi bi-sliders" aria-hidden="true"></i>Tools</h2>
            <p class="settings-group__intro">How every tool behaves and shows its text.</p>
            {{ switchSetting("settingLive", "Live typing", "Tools convert as you type, without pressing their button. Each tool's own switch changes this too.") }}
            {{ switchSetting("settingConvrtrsLive", "Live typing in Convrtrs", "Convrtrs has its own switch, as converting into every format at once can be slow on long text.") }}
            {{ switchSetting("settingAboutOpen", "Open “More about this tool” to start with", "Show each tool's examples and links without opening the fold.") }}
            {{ switchSetting("settingMono", "Monospace text in the boxes", "Every character takes the same width, so hex, binary and Morse line up in columns.") }}
            <div class="setting">
                <div class="setting__text">
                    <span class="setting__name" id="settingBoxSize-label">Text size in the boxes</span>
                    <small class="setting__hint" id="settingBoxSize-hint">For long puzzle data, or reading on a small screen.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="setting__end">
                    {{ savedNote("settingBoxSize") }}
                    <div class="setting-segments setting__control" role="group" aria-labelledby="settingBoxSize-label" aria-describedby="settingBoxSize-hint" id="settingBoxSize">
                        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-value="small">Smaller</button>
                        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-value="normal">Normal</button>
                        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-value="large">Larger</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="setting">
                <div class="setting__text">
                    <label class="setting__name" for="settingDelimiter">Hex delimiter</label>
                    <small class="setting__hint" id="settingDelimiter-hint">What goes between bytes when a tool writes hex. Each tool's delimiter dropdown starts on this.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="setting__end">
                    {{ savedNote("settingDelimiter") }}
                    <div class="setting__control">{{ delimiter("setting") }}</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="settings-group" id="categories" aria-labelledby="categories-title">
            <h2 class="settings-group__title" id="categories-title"><i class="bi bi-grid" aria-hidden="true"></i>Category pages</h2>
            <p class="settings-group__intro">A category page, such as Cipher tools, lists all its tools one after another. Choose which start open; the rest start collapsed to their name, and you can open them on the page.</p>
            {%- for link in nav %}
            {%- if link.excludeFromSettings == false %}
            <details class="tool-fold settings-category" data-settings-category="{{ link.id }}" data-category-name="{{ link.label }}">
                <summary>
                    <i class="bi bi-chevron-right tool-fold__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ link.label }}{{ savedNote("category-" ~ link.id) }}
                    <small data-category-count></small>
                </summary>
                <div class="settings-category__body">
                    <div class="settings-category__actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" data-open-all>Open all<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ link.label }}</span></button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" data-close-all>Close all<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ link.label }}</span></button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="settings-category__tools">
                        {%- for child in link.children | sort(false, true, "label") %}
                        <label class="settings-tool">
                            <span>{{ child.label }}</span>
                            <span class="form-check form-switch m-0">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" data-tool-key="{{ link.id }}/{{ child.id }}" data-tool-name="{{ child.label }}" aria-label="{{ child.label }} starts open">
                            </span>
                        </label>
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            </details>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="settings-group" id="data" aria-labelledby="data-title">
            <h2 class="settings-group__title" id="data-title"><i class="bi bi-database" aria-hidden="true"></i>Your data</h2>
            <p class="settings-group__intro">Settings are saved in this browser's local storage. Nothing is sent anywhere, and nothing you type into a tool is saved.</p>
            <div class="settings-data" id="settingsData"></div>
            <div class="settings-data__actions">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-danger btn-icon-text" id="settingsReset"><i class="bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise" aria-hidden="true"></i>Reset all settings</button>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" href="/community/privacy/">What we store and why</a>
            </div>
            <p class="settings-data__undo" id="settingsUndo" hidden>
                All settings are back to how they start.
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" id="settingsUndoButton">Undo</button>
            </p>
        </section>

        <p class="visually-hidden" role="status" id="settingsStatus"></p>
    </div>
</section>
<script type="module" src="/assets/js/site/settings.js"></script>
